msgid "This file contains a pattern found in hacked websites. Some premium plugins and themes use similar tricks to hide their code, so check where the file comes from."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Security/Findings.php:111
msgid "If the file isn’t part of a plugin or theme you installed on purpose, it’s likely malware: restore the plugin or theme from a fresh copy, delete files you don’t recognize, then change your WordPress, hosting and database passwords. If it’s from a product you trust, mark it as expected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Security/Findings.php:115
msgid "ClamAV’s database of known malware matched this file: it’s code from a known hacking campaign or tool, not just a suspicious pattern, so the site has very likely been hacked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Security/Findings.php:116
#: includes/Security/Findings.php:121
msgid "Restore the plugin or theme the file belongs to from a fresh copy, or delete the file if nothing you installed needs it. Then change your WordPress, hosting and database passwords, and look for how it got in (an outdated plugin, a nulled theme or a stolen password). Ask your host or a security specialist if more files are affected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Security/Findings.php:120
msgid "This exact file was found to be malware by a deep scan on another website Arva SEO checks: it’s code from a known hacking campaign or tool, not just a suspicious pattern, so the site has very likely been hacked."
